  "summary": "The identified studies apply transformer-based architectures, specifically self-attention encoder models, to the domain of energy demand forecasting, operationalized as predicting electricity consumption [V0126, V0127, V0128, V0125]. These models are evaluated across diverse datasets including ProtMap, FireScope, ChurnBench, and GridWatch, with reported performance metrics ranging from MAE values of 0.93 to accuracy and F1 scores around 0.86 and 0.72 respectively [V0126, V0125, V0128]. Additionally, a comparative study on predicting electricity consumption utilizes decentralised training without pooled records, evaluated on the FireScope dataset [V0131].",
